From b0399bcbb11447e967ceaacadb34b4a383f5cdc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gaia <build@heygaia.io>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 08:05:29 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(css): :focus, :focus-visible and :focus-within match the
 focused element

The focus pseudo-classes never matched: querySelector(':focus') was null,
matches(':focus-within') false, and focus styles never applied, though the
page had a focused element. The page's focus model now records the focused
element (and whether it is focus-visible: keyboard or script focus, or a
pointer press on a control that takes typed text) on the document, and
selectors match :focus on it and on a shadow host holding it, and
:focus-within on its shadow-including ancestors.

A focus move restyles only the elements whose state flipped and only for
rules whose compound can select them (state dependencies now keep the
compound's key), so moving focus between fields of one form does not
re-cascade the document; the retained result matches a full cascade.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tm2SNEJ42hMPiZ6cFb8Vih
